### File Responsibilities

1. [`motor_protocol.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/motor_protocol.py) *(new extracted module)*:
   - Owns polynomial CRC32, packet encode/decode functions, protocol constants, and error types.
   - Owns `IM6014Transceiver`: encapsulates stream buffering, sliding-window `b'\xfc\xee'` framing, candidate rejection/recovery, timeout capping, and timeout restoration.
   - Exposes compatibility wrappers so existing callers and signatures remain identical.
2. [`spin_5rpm.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/spin_5rpm.py) *(preserved entry point)*:
   - Imports and re-exports `command`, `feedback`, `exchange`, `healthy`, `crc32`, `PORT`, `RATIO`, and bounds from [`motor_protocol.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/motor_protocol.py).
   - Retains CLI argument parsing, motion ramping, and shutdown logging.
3. [`motor_session.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/motor_session.py) *(preserved GUI session)*:
   - Imports packet functions and `exchange` into module namespace (preserving `test_startup` monkeypatch).
   - Retains `DemoSerial` and worker loop without modification to public UI contracts.
4. [`test_motor_protocol.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/test_motor_protocol.py) *(new test file for B01–B10)*:
   - Provides `FakeSerialTransport` with scripted chunks, recorded writes, and deadline instrumentation.
   - Implements independent test suites for B01–B10.
5. [`scripts/check_offline_baseline.sh`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/scripts/check_offline_baseline.sh) and [`test_startup.py`](file:///home/sid/Documents/code/im6014Workbench/test_startup.py):
   - Adds `motor_protocol.py` and `test_motor_protocol.py` to the copy list and fingerprint sets.

